  "evidence": "Checked the single written occurrence of the exact name SBig and both PVBig occurrences in the complete Lean archive. Followed the selected rank, modular evaluation and SLayer paths from their named consumers, and derived the kernel of the quotient map from the two ranges in sha_le.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "FCT-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "The selected odd-cycle count runs over the enlarged field",
      "anchor": "inputs-field-cycle-interfaces",
      "statement": "The selected arithmetic count applies bOdd_zk to integral filtered odd-degree homology in the field where the matrix groups live. In the degree-two application this field is the auxiliary cyclotomic layer L′. Data in a further field F realize cycles over 𝒪_{L′} with coefficients ℤ/ℓ^ν.",
      "hypotheses": "Twist E≥1, ℓ prime, L totally complex with HasMuQ. The chosen L′ has 2E+1<r₂(L′) and 2E+1<ℓ^c for its maximal root depth c. The subsequent group and character calculation assumes Lay ℓ c ν ζ γ for F/L′.",
      "definitions": [
        "SBig is an implication between real primitive-cycle boundary statements. Its name has a single occurrence in the archived Lean text, at its own definition. The neighboring PVBig uses odd k, hence even cycle degree k+1.",
        "In the selected BStarOdd/SUpper path, k is even and m=k+1 is odd. The matrix degree in the application is m=2E+1, and the stable size used by the count is 4E+6.",
        "IsPrim describes a real cycle via the diagonal minus the two coordinate inclusions. IsPrimFam describes a family Φ of finite-coefficient evaluations vanishing on boundaries, invariant under stabilization and linear in block multiplicity.",
        "The relevant count compares the values of ℓ^{2E}Φ and uses adjacent homology torsion degrees 2E+1 and 2E at the same stable size."
      ],
