    {
      "id": "FCT-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Inclusion of two endomorphism images descends the bound on the locally trivial length",
      "anchor": "inputs-field-cycle-quotient",
      "statement": "For d=ℓ^a and a cyclotomic layer L′/L, the tower description of shaInv in positive twist E compares M/(g^d−1)M with M/(g−1)M. The projection induced by identity on representatives is surjective; its kernel is (g−1)M/(g^d−1)M. Hence shaInv(L,ℓ,E)≤shaInv(L′,ℓ,E).",
      "hypotheses": "L is a number field with HasMuQ, ℓ prime and E≥1; the numerical use starts with L totally complex. The choice of cyclotomic generator and common tower module is given by exists_descends. Length takes values in ℕ∞ before a finiteness bound is available.",
      "definitions": [
        "M=Xinf ℓ ℓ ⊤ over the base algebraic closure; g=xTw ℓ ℓ ⊤ E γ, the dual action of the chosen lift twisted by χ_cyc(γ)^E.",
        "shaInv is the ℤ_ℓ-length of the locally trivial absolute degree-one group for (ℚ_ℓ/ℤ_ℓ)(−E), with constraints on decomposition groups above ℓ and inertia outside ℓ.",
        "The projection of cokernel models is induced by range(g^d−1)⊆range(g−1). The comparison of the two lengths then feeds the finite bound on the base field.",
        "Example L=ℚ(ζ₃), E=1: the chosen relative degree is 9 and L′=ℚ(ζ₂₇). In the distinct rank-one module example g=4 on ℤ₃, the quotient map is ℤ/27→ℤ/3."
      ],
